---
title: "Free Tool to Blur Faces in Photos Online"
description: "Blur, pixelate or black out faces in a photo. Click a face to keep it visible. Face detection runs in your browser. Your photo is never uploaded."
---

<section class="tool-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <%= partial "partials/brand" %>
    <h1>Face Blur</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Hide every face in a photo in seconds.
      Face detection runs on your device. Your photo is never uploaded.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tool">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="model-bar" id="model" data-state="loading">
      <div class="model-text">
        <strong>AI</strong>
        <span class="status" id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading…</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="drop" id="drop">
      <p class="drop-title">Drop a photo here</p>
      <p class="drop-text">or paste it, or choose a file. JPG, PNG and WebP.</p>
      <div class="drop-actions">
        <label class="button">
          Choose a photo
          <input type="file" id="file" accept="image/*" class="visually-hidden">
        </label>
        <button type="button" id="sample" class="button button-outline">Try an example photo</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="editor" id="editor" hidden>
      <div class="controls control-row">
        <div class="control">
          <span class="control-label">Style</span>
          <div class="chips" id="style">
            <button type="button" class="chip" data-value="blur" aria-pressed="true">Blur</button>
            <button type="button" class="chip" data-value="pixelate" aria-pressed="false">Pixelate</button>
            <button type="button" class="chip" data-value="box" aria-pressed="false">Black box</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <label class="control" id="strength-control">
          <span class="control-label">Strength</span>
          <input type="range" id="strength" min="1" max="10" value="8">
        </label>
        <div class="control">
          <span class="control-label">Shape</span>
          <div class="chips" id="shape">
            <button type="button" class="chip" data-value="oval" aria-pressed="true">Oval</button>
            <button type="button" class="chip" data-value="rect" aria-pressed="false">Rectangle</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="stage">
        <canvas id="canvas" aria-label="Photo with faces hidden"></canvas>
        <div class="boxes" id="boxes"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="editor-foot">
        <div class="editor-actions">
          <button type="button" id="new" class="button button-outline">Use another photo</button>
          <button type="button" id="original" class="button button-outline">Hold to see original</button>
          <button type="button" id="download" class="button" disabled>Download photo</button>
        </div>
        <p class="download-note" id="download-note" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="notes">
      <div>
        <h3>Private by design</h3>
        <p>The page has no server code. The face model, <a href="https://github.com/opencv/opencv_zoo/tree/main/models/face_detection_yunet" target="_blank" rel="noopener">YuNet</a> from OpenCV (MIT license), is 230 KB and runs on your device.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Check before you share</h3>
        <p>Very small, turned or covered faces can be missed. Look at the whole photo. Drag on it to hide anything else, such as a name badge or a reflection.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Location data removed</h3>
        <p>The downloaded photo is a new file. It does not keep the original's metadata, such as GPS location, camera model and date.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script type="module" src="/javascripts/tools/face-blur.js"></script>
